WEBVTT

00:00:05.125 --> 00:00:06.417
Hmm...

00:00:11.042 --> 00:00:12.125
Hmm?

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.417
Thank you for holding.
Your call is...

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.083
- ..moderately...
- ..important to us.

00:01:30.417 --> 00:01:34.208
- Where's he going to sleep?
- Not in my room. He's a he.

00:01:34.292 --> 00:01:36.292
- Tony's a he.
- Shut up.

00:01:36.417 --> 00:01:38.833
And Tony would be more than welcome
to a bunk-up.

00:01:38.917 --> 00:01:40.458
- Who's Tony?
- I'm warning you.

00:01:40.542 --> 00:01:43.958
- Just some boy she's in love with.
- No? Darling, really?

00:01:44.042 --> 00:01:46.500
- That's it!
- When can I meet him?

00:01:46.625 --> 00:01:48.125
Can I meet him? Darling?

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:56.875
- He can sleep in my room.
- He's not sleeping in anyone's room.

00:01:56.958 --> 00:01:59.458
He's going in the attic.
I want you all to lock your doors.

00:01:59.542 --> 00:02:02.250
I can't find anything
about an English explorer in Peru.

00:02:02.292 --> 00:02:04.083
- Of course you can't.
- Why not?

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:08.208
He's making the whole thing up. It's the
sort of sob story your mother falls for.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.583
- Hang on. That's not fair.
- It so is fair.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:13.333
You've literally just brought home
a random bear.

00:02:13.458 --> 00:02:16.083
- So embarrassing.
- You'd have done the same thing.

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:18.333
We're much more similar than you think.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.292
- What are you doing?
- The storm is upon us.

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:25.875
Oh, you and your knees.
I can tell you for a fact, Mrs Bird,

00:02:25.958 --> 00:02:27.708
it is not going to rain indoors.

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:34.875
- Oh, no.
- There she blows.

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:38.583
- Mr Brown, are you there?
- Yes, hello.

00:02:38.708 --> 00:02:40.417
Yes, that sounds fine.

00:02:40.542 --> 00:02:43.167
No, no, no, don't read me
the terms and conditions.

00:02:43.208 --> 00:02:47.833
I want to action this as soon as possible.
Don't put me on hold again!

00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:50.333
Paddington? What is going on in there?

00:02:50.458 --> 00:02:55.417
Er, nothing. I'm just having
a spot of bother with the facilities.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.333
Erm... Nice weather for the ducks?

00:03:25.792 --> 00:03:26.583
Oh.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.750
That was amazing.

00:03:34.625 --> 00:03:38.333
Dear Aunt Lucy.
I have arrived in London

00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:43.792
and so far it has rained, poured,
drizzled and chucked it down.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.292
And I miss you.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.542
London is not how we imagined it.

00:03:51.083 --> 00:03:54.125
Hardly anyone says hello
or wears hats.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:58.083
And you can no longer simply
turn up at the station and get a home.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.292
It's hard to see where a bear
could ever belong

00:04:01.375 --> 00:04:03.583
in such a strange, cold city.

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:09.083
Luckily, I met the Browns, who are
letting me sleep in their attic.

00:04:09.125 --> 00:04:12.625
They have a lovely house, but I'm not
going to be allowed to stay.

00:04:12.708 --> 00:04:15.500
That animal is going
straight to the authorities.

00:04:15.583 --> 00:04:18.667
- What about the explorer?
- There is no explorer.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:22.375
I'm not putting this family in danger
while you go on some wild-goose chase.

00:04:22.458 --> 00:04:25.333
First thing tomorrow,
that bear is out of here.

00:04:25.417 --> 00:04:28.875
The Browns are a very curious tribe.

00:04:28.958 --> 00:04:31.625
Mr Brown is something called
a risk analyst.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:36.208
He says that having a bear in the house
increases the chances of major disaster

00:04:36.292 --> 00:04:37.875
by 4,000%.

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:43.583
Mrs Brown illustrates
adventure stories.

00:04:44.125 --> 00:04:47.500
Her latest is set in the old tunnels
and sewers under London.

00:04:48.042 --> 00:04:49.750
She says she's stuck at the moment

00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:52.333
because she can't imagine
what her hero looks like,

00:04:52.708 --> 00:04:55.958
but has no trouble coming up with
nicknames for her daughter Judy,

00:04:56.042 --> 00:04:59.958
- like "twinkle" and "coconut" and...
- Sweety pops? Hello, darling.

00:05:00.042 --> 00:05:02.625
I was thinking of going
to the sewers tomorrow night.

00:05:02.708 --> 00:05:07.667
I just wondered if you wanted
to join me. You could bring this Tony.

00:05:08.292 --> 00:05:10.875
Why would I want to bring anyone
down the toilet?

00:05:10.958 --> 00:05:12.792
Come on, darling, it's not like that.

00:05:12.875 --> 00:05:17.000
It's a subterranean labyrinth
that can take you anywhere in the city.

00:05:17.042 --> 00:05:19.500
It's weird, it smells
and it's embarrassing.

00:05:19.625 --> 00:05:21.833
Sure. Good point.

00:05:21.917 --> 00:05:24.417
Judy suffers
from a serious condition

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:25.875
called "embarrassment".

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.167
She is seeing a boy called Tony
but won't bring him home.

00:05:29.208 --> 00:05:33.000
- So, when can I come round your house?
- That's never gonna happen.

00:05:33.583 --> 00:05:35.042
She is learning Chinese...

00:05:35.083 --> 00:05:38.667
Could you tell me the way
to the central business district?

00:05:39.375 --> 00:05:42.792
..so she can run away
and start a small business.

00:05:42.917 --> 00:05:45.042
I have been accused
of insider trading

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:47.792
and require legal representation.

00:05:47.875 --> 00:05:51.167
When Jonathan grows up,
he wants to be an astronaut.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.708
Last year he built
a pair of rocket boots...

00:05:53.792 --> 00:05:56.208
Three, two, one.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.458
And is now only allowed to play

00:05:59.542 --> 00:06:03.667
with safe, educational, indoor toys
from the olden days.

00:06:05.792 --> 00:06:09.083
They live with
an old relative called Mrs Bird.

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:13.000
Her husband was in the Navy, and she
still likes everything shipshape.

00:06:14.833 --> 00:06:18.000
Tomorrow, they are taking me
to the authorities,

00:06:18.042 --> 00:06:21.292
who will house me in something
that is not an orphanage,

00:06:21.375 --> 00:06:25.750
but still doesn't sound like the sort
of home we were really hoping for.

00:06:28.542 --> 00:06:29.792
Can't you sleep?

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:32.458
Me neither.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:35.792
I do wish
we could have found the explorer.

00:06:35.833 --> 00:06:38.833
I know, Paddington.
But I've been looking everywhere

00:06:38.875 --> 00:06:42.208
and I still can't find any mention
of an English expedition to Peru.

00:06:42.458 --> 00:06:46.625
But there really was an explorer,
Mrs Brown. He gave my uncle this hat.

00:06:46.708 --> 00:06:48.833
What, that was the explorer's hat?

00:06:49.083 --> 00:06:50.917
Hm-hmm. Why?

00:06:51.792 --> 00:06:55.292
I've got a friend who runs
an antiques shop in the Portobello Road.

00:06:55.375 --> 00:06:57.083
He knows all about old things
like your hat.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:58.708
Oh...

00:06:58.792 --> 00:07:01.458
It's just possible
he could help us find your explorer.

00:07:01.542 --> 00:07:03.250
Well, that would be wonderful.

00:07:03.333 --> 00:07:06.750
- But didn't Mr Brown say...
- Don't you worry about Mr Brown.

00:07:06.792 --> 00:07:09.958
As far as he's concerned,
we're going to the authorities.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:13.583
But I'm not standing by while there's
a chance of finding you a proper home.

00:07:14.917 --> 00:07:17.083
Now make sure you get some sleep, OK?

